{"qid":"Q189","names":["Republic of Iceland"],"title":"Republic of Iceland","endonym":{"native":"Ísland","lang":"is"},"capsule":"The Republic of Iceland was proclaimed at Þingvellir on 17 June 1944, severing the personal union with Denmark that had been suspended in practice since Germany's occupation of Denmark in April 1940. Sveinn Björnsson, who had served as regent since 1941, became the first president. Iceland joined NATO in 1949 as a founding member, hosting the American Keflavík air base through the Cold War; successive Cod Wars (1958–1976) extended Iceland's exclusive fishing zone to 200 nautical miles. The country developed one of the world's highest per-capita incomes on the basis of fishing and geothermal energy before its three major banks collapsed in 2008 with combined liabilities roughly ten times GDP, requiring an IMF assistance program.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Iceland's territory is precisely defined and uncontested; the dataset from date of 1946 post-dates the 1944 proclamation and likely reflects a data source artifact or recognition lag.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Iceland","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Iceland"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Iceland","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iceland"}],"britannica":"place/Iceland","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Iceland","rulers":[{"qid":"Q207206","name":"Sveinn Björnsson","start":1944,"end":1952,"image":"Sveinn Björnsson.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sveinn%20Bj%C3%B6rnsson.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Forseti.is","attributionRequired